:"1784921168127435001-29d7f9fa-a836-475f-a352-306490b89779"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8d93a784d6d618c5f2c34c88e88c10062bc27586bad30b051e5fd656c37028fa","event_uuid":"95705d83-c79e-4dcb-ae48-0f9ee3b89eb6","position":{"commit_sha":"d4336c3156b2c230457cf2736727c95396398ece","position":"1784921645291497788-95705d83-c79e-4dcb-ae48-0f9ee3b89eb6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"02a2beeb984c2078534a5e92fe36864058b89222355da3918c7ba4bd5d55f426","event_uuid":"da4d31f5-c2ea-4c29-ba82-2d7e94859a1d","position":{"commit_sha":"5f7e2dc75a941ce49685b49a113efa2741d48309","position":"1784924786460343001-da4d31f5-c2ea-4c29-ba82-2d7e94859a1d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1784669766382049001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"734cf7b3-b191-4a63-bc7e-60a0f9525417","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"fc72-bf7e-7652-4228"},{"link_uuid":"da4d31f5-c2ea-4c29-ba82-2d7e94859a1d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"13f6-4d3e-b572-49a6"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`CodeReviewBatchRunner.run` iterates only the static `req.criteria` list and stamps each finding\nwith `reviewer_id = prompt_id` and no logical criterion id\n(`src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py:49,79`). The code-review gate YAML injects only the 13\nbuilt-in overlays (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/code-review.yaml:77-94,109-126`), so an activated\nproject criterion never enters Round A/B and, even if it did, its findings could not be attributed\nto `project.<name>`. Plan-review already solves the related dynamic-membership problem at runtime\n(`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:206-225`). Code review differs because its\nsingle runner serves both `round_a` and `round_b`; project fan-in must therefore be explicitly\nonce-only. This is the second of five seams (root cause on superseded bug 8a4b).\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a Round-A-only project-criteria input to the existing code-review runner:\n\n- At the code-review batch assembly point in `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` (where\n  `CodeReviewBatchRunner` is constructed around `gate_dispatch.py:643-645` and `repo_root` is\n  available as `request.repo_root`), read `registry.effective_criteria(repo_root)` plus\n  `registry.effective_routing(repo_root)`. Select active `project.` ids whose routing entry has\n  `exec: LLM`; DET-tier project criteria remain outside this LLM finder path. Resolve each physical\n  prompt with `criterion_prompt_id(cid, gate_key=\"code_review\")`\n  `[rebar:fc72-bf7e-7652-4228]` and build entries carrying both `prompt` and logical `criterion_id`.\n- Extend `CodeReviewBatchRunner.__init__` with an additive default-empty `project_criteria` tuple.\n  `run()` combines `req.criteria` with those entries only when `req.step_id == \"round_a\"`; for\n  `round_b` it uses only `req.criteria`. The runner instance may therefore serve both YAML batch\n  steps without double execution. Activated project criteria are deliberately once-per-review\n  opt-ins rather than recommendation/glob-driven built-ins, so they run in Round A and do not\n  consume or bypass the Round-B escalation cap of three. No seen-set or cross-run mutable state is\n  used, keeping retries/replays deterministic.\n- When a project entry emits findings, preserve any model-emitted `criteria` tags and append the\n  logical `criterion_id` once if absent; keep the existing physical `reviewer_id` provenance.\n- If an activated project criterion prompt is missing or malformed, fail loudly with a located\n  `LLMError` naming the logical criterion and expected\n  `.rebar/prompts/<physical-prompt-id>.md` path. Errors reading or validating\n  `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` are not swallowed or degraded to built-ins: the shared criteria\n  loader error propagates, so invalid project configuration cannot silently disable review.\n\n**Rejected alternatives.** Adding static project slots to `code-review.yaml` cannot work because\nproject ids are repository-specific. Appending project entries to every `BatchRunRequest` would\nexecute them in both rounds. A mutable seen-set would make retries and replay depend on call order.\nThe Round-A-only branch on the stable YAML step id is explicit, stateless, and testable.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` — assemble active LLM project entries and pass them to\n  the runner.\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py` — accept project entries; inject them in Round A\n  only; append logical criteria ids; raise a located prompt error.\n- `tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py` — extend the shared file; add a synthetic repo\n  fixture that activates `project.foo` and writes\n  `.rebar/prompts/code-review-project-foo.md`, reused by later children.\n\n`BatchRunRequest`, the workflow interpreter, YAML membership, Pass-3 routing, and the Round-B cap\nare unchanged. Pass-3 project posture is owned by dependent child 58ef.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path plus workflow boundary (`fan_in`): run the real two-round workflow with a stub finder;\n  `project.foo` executes exactly once in `round_a`, never in `round_b`, and every emitted finding\n  retains existing tags plus logical id `project.foo`.\n- Direct runner edge: invoking a `round_b` request with project entries configured does not append\n  or execute them; replaying a `round_a` request produces the same once-per-call plan without\n  retained mutable state.\n- Parity: an overlay-absent repo produces the same ordered built-in Round-A/Round-B requests and\n  findings as before; no project entries are present.\n- Config error (`missing`): active `project.foo` with no prompt raises a located `LLMError` naming\n  both `project.foo` and `.rebar/prompts/code-review-project-foo.md`.\n\nTier: unit plus an offline workflow integration using the real interpreter and stubbed agent calls.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] An activated LLM-tier project criterion executes exactly once across the complete Round-A +\n      Round-B workflow, in Round A, and each finding preserves prior tags while carrying logical\n      `project.<name>`; verified by\n      `rtk .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py -k fan_in`.\n- [ ] An overlay-absent repo yields the unchanged ordered built-in batches and findings; verified by\n      `rtk .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py -k parity`.\n- [ ] A project criterion with a missing prompt raises a located `LLMError` naming the criterion and\n      expected path; verified by\n      `rtk .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py -k missing`.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"Assemble effective project criteria; thread into code-review runner"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py","reason":"Iterate project criteria; stamp logical criteria id; located error on missing prompt"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py","reason":"Fan-in/parity/config-error tests + synthetic-repo fixture"}],"keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","fc72-bf7e-7652-4228"],["parent","119f-63e3-34b7-4f96"],["relates_to","13f6-4d3e-b572-49a6"]],"parent_id":"119f-63e3-34b7-4f96","parent_status_uuid":"2291024b-a687-4bfb-8c8e-f748f1bdb308","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["review-architecture","project-criteria","integration"],"ticket_id":"761e-5af2-ed57-408a","ticket_type":"story","title":"Fan project criteria into Round A/B and attribute logical ids","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4d4137ed-faf2-433b-a658-b65d5927ccb5","4216625f-1321-4a3a-bd3a-d1de929c6f1e","734cf7b3-b191-4a63-bc7e-60a0f9525417","462e4349-5935-4ed7-8c34-2e1004cdbbb2","7e22f9d3-9df8-49c8-b15a-390152dda20d","eddcc3f0-e000-435f-9eaf-ad2812e7e8da","2291024b-a687-4bfb-8c8e-f748f1bdb308","29d7f9fa-a836-475f-a352-306490b89779","95705d83-c79e-4dcb-ae48-0f9ee3b89eb6","da4d31f5-c2ea-4c29-ba82-2d7e94859a1d"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1784924786460343002,"uuid":"bf5a2c80-cacb-4edb-9490-5b861fb537ee"}